        <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl lg:text-4xl text-ink leading-tight mb-5">What is Depression? How Is It Different from Sadness?</h1>
        <p class="text-ink-muted text-lg leading-relaxed">Everyone feels sad from time to time. But depression is far more than that — it is a clinical condition that can last for weeks, months or even years, profoundly affecting daily life.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-12 bg-white">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-5 lg:px-8">
        <div class="prose-custom space-y-8">

          <div>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">The difference between sadness and depression</h2>
            <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">Sadness is usually a temporary emotion triggered by a specific event — a loss, disappointment or failure. It eases with time and support, and the person retains some enjoyment of life.</p>
            <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Depression is different: the low mood does not lift, it persists without a clear cause or out of proportion to circumstances, and the person can no longer enjoy things they once found pleasurable. This disrupts everyday functioning.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-primary/5 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-primary/15">
            <p class="text-sm text-ink font-medium mb-2">DSM-5 diagnostic criterion: the two-week rule</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">A diagnosis of Major Depressive Disorder requires that at least five of the symptoms listed below are present nearly every day for an uninterrupted period of two weeks. One of those symptoms must be either depressed mood or loss of interest or pleasure.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">Symptoms of depression</h2>
            <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-4 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <p class="text-xs font-medium text-ink mb-2">Emotional</p>
                <ul class="text-xs text-ink-muted space-y-1.5">
                  <li>• Persistent sadness or emptiness</li>
                  <li>• Loss of interest or pleasure</li>
                  <li>• Feelings of worthlessness</li>
                  <li>• Excessive guilt</li>
                  <li>• Hopelessness, helplessness</li>
                  <li>• Thoughts of death or suicide</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-4 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <p class="text-xs font-medium text-ink mb-2">Cognitive</p>
                <ul class="text-xs text-ink-muted space-y-1.5">
                  <li>• Difficulty concentrating</li>
                  <li>• Trouble making decisions</li>
                  <li>• Negative thought patterns</li>
                  <li>• Memory problems</li>
                  <li>• Self-criticism</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-4 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <p class="text-xs font-medium text-ink mb-2">Physical</p>
                <ul class="text-xs text-ink-muted space-y-1.5">
                  <li>• Sleep changes (too much or too little)</li>
                  <li>• Appetite changes</li>
                  <li>• Fatigue, loss of energy</li>
                  <li>• Psychomotor slowing</li>
                  <li>• Unexplained aches and pains</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">Types of depression</h2>
            <div class="space-y-3">
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-5 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-1.5">Major Depressive Disorder</h3>
                <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">The most widely recognised type. Symptoms last at least two weeks and significantly impair daily functioning. Episodes may recur.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-5 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-1.5">Dysthymia (Persistent Depressive Disorder)</h3>
                <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">A milder but chronic form of depression lasting at least two years. The feeling of "I've always been this way" is common.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-5 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-1.5">Seasonal Affective Disorder</h3>
                <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Begins in autumn–winter and resolves in spring. More prevalent in northern countries and regions with limited sunlight.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-5 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-1.5">Postpartum Depression</h3>
                <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Develops after childbirth and is far more severe and prolonged than the "baby blues". It affects approximately 10–15% of mothers.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-primary/5 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-primary/15">
            <p class="text-sm text-ink font-medium mb-2">Global scale</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">According to the World Health Organisation, approximately 280 million people worldwide are living with depression, making it one of the most prevalent mental health conditions globally. (WHO, 2023)</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">Causes</h2>
            <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">Depression cannot be attributed to a single cause. It is understood within a biopsychosocial model:</p>
            <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-4 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <p class="text-xs font-medium text-ink mb-2">Biological</p>
                <ul class="text-xs text-ink-muted space-y-1.5">
                  <li>• Genetic predisposition</li>
                  <li>• Serotonin and dopamine imbalances</li>
                  <li>• Thyroid and hormonal issues</li>
                  <li>• Chronic illness</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-4 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <p class="text-xs font-medium text-ink mb-2">Psychological</p>
                <ul class="text-xs text-ink-muted space-y-1.5">
                  <li>• Negative thought schemas</li>
                  <li>• Low self-efficacy</li>
                  <li>• Past trauma or losses</li>
                  <li>• Perfectionism</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-4 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <p class="text-xs font-medium text-ink mb-2">Social</p>
                <ul class="text-xs text-ink-muted space-y-1.5">
                  <li>• Loneliness, isolation</li>
                  <li>• Relationship difficulties</li>
                  <li>• Work or financial stress</li>
                  <li>• Weak support network</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">Treatment options</h2>
            <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">Depression is a condition that can largely be overcome with the right support. The main evidence-based approaches include:</p>
            <ul class="space-y-3">
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg>
                <div>
                  <p class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">Cognitive Behavioural Therapy (CBT)</p>
                  <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted mt-0.5">Focuses on identifying and changing the negative thought patterns that fuel depression. CBT has the broadest research base of any therapy approach for treating depression.</p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg>
                <div>
                  <p class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">Antidepressant Medication</p>
                  <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted mt-0.5">Prescribed following psychiatric evaluation. For moderate to severe depression, combining medication with therapy generally yields the best outcomes.</p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg>
                <div>
                  <p class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">EMDR and Trauma-Focused Therapy</p>
                  <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted mt-0.5">Addresses underlying traumatic experiences to support long-term recovery from depression.</p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg>
                <div>
                  <p class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">Lifestyle Changes</p>
                  <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted mt-0.5">Regular exercise, sleep hygiene and social connection are important factors that support the treatment process.</p>
                </div>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-accent/5 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-accent/15">
            <p class="text-sm text-ink font-medium mb-2">If you are having thoughts of harming yourself or others</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Please contact a healthcare provider or someone you trust immediately. These thoughts are a symptom of depression and can improve with help.</p>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
